The levelised cost of solar PV fell from $0.378/kWh in 2010 to $0.049/kWh in 2022 — a learning rate that exceeds even semiconductor chips.
Countries that invested early in renewables — Denmark, Germany, Spain — are now major exporters of wind turbines, solar panels, and grid management technology, creating lasting industrial advantage.
Rural economies benefit disproportionately: wind and solar lease payments are providing reliable income for farmers and landowners in regions with few other economic opportunities.
The US Inflation Reduction Act's $369 billion clean energy investment has already triggered $3 trillion in private sector announcements — proving policy certainty unlocks enormous capital.
Oil price shocks (1973, 1979, 2022) cause global recessions; a renewables-based economy is immune to fossil fuel price volatility, improving macro-economic stability.
